<IndustryPage {...pageData}>
<p>UK property management companies are caught between demanding landlords and expectant tenants. Landlords want transparent reporting and minimal void periods. Tenants want quick maintenance responses and easy communication. Property managers are stuck in the middle, juggling phone calls, email chains, spreadsheets, and a property management system that handles tenancy admin but can't deliver the digital experience either side now expects. Bespoke software can change that - but most companies are still operating with tools that were adequate a decade ago and are now a competitive liability.</p>
<p>Off-the-shelf property management software handles the basics - tenancy records, rent scheduling, and basic reporting - but falls short in the areas that actually differentiate your service. Generic maintenance modules assign jobs but don't track contractor performance or give tenants real-time updates. Landlord reporting is typically a monthly exercise involving spreadsheet exports and manual formatting, which means landlords get stale information and your team loses hours every month. Arrears management is a spreadsheet, deposit protection deadlines are tracked in a calendar, and inspection reports are still paper forms or Word documents with embedded photos that are impossible to search later.</p>
<p>We build custom software for UK property management companies that fits the way your portfolio actually operates. Whether it's a tenant maintenance platform that accepts issues with photos, automatically assigns them to approved contractors, and updates tenants at every stage, a rent collection system that automates reminders and tracks arrears with real-time rent roll visibility, or a landlord portal that generates financial and operational reports on demand without your team lifting a finger, bespoke software eliminates the manual workarounds that consume your team's day. We integrate with your existing systems - Alto, CFP, Sage, Xero - so data flows automatically and nothing is duplicated.</p>
<p>Property compliance carries serious consequences. Deposit protection deadlines under the Housing Act 2004, right-to-rent checks under the Immigration Act 2014, gas safety certificates, EPC requirements, and Section 21 notice validity all demand precise timing and documentation. A single missed deadline can invalidate a Section 21 notice or result in a deposit protection penalty of up to three times the deposit amount. Bespoke software can track every compliance date with automated alerts, generate legal notices with the correct statutory wording, and maintain a complete audit trail per property - replacing the calendar reminders and spreadsheet trackers that leave property management companies exposed to legal and financial risk.</p>
<p>A UK letting agency managing 400 properties was spending two full days per month producing landlord reports and losing tenants to competitors who offered online maintenance reporting. Their existing property management software couldn't produce customised landlord statements or accept maintenance requests online. We built a bespoke platform with a landlord reporting portal and tenant maintenance app. Landlord report preparation dropped from two days to under two hours, tenant satisfaction scores improved significantly, and the agency won two new portfolio instructions specifically because of the digital experience they could offer landlords.</p>
<p>Property management is a sector where bespoke software delivers clear ROI. Every tenancy, every maintenance job, and every rent payment generates data. The opportunity is building software that turns that data into reduced void periods, automated workflows, and the transparent reporting that wins and retains landlord business.</p>

